; administration has no dependency contract: SRS §6.4 grants it "all (read via
; interfaces)". The privacy contracts below still constrain HOW it reads —
; through services and dto, never another module's models.

; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
; 2. Module internals are private — SRS §6.5 rule 1.
;
;   "Cross-module imports are permitted only from apps.<module>.services and
;    apps.<module>.dto — never from apps.<module>.models."
;
; One contract per module, protecting its internals from every other module.
; Extended beyond `models` to every non-public submodule, because reaching
; into another module's selectors or domain breaks the seam just as thoroughly.
;
; DIRECT IMPORTS ONLY. Every contract below sets `allow_indirect_imports = True`,
; which makes import-linter report only imports named in an import statement.
; Without it SRS §6.5 rule 1 is unsatisfiable rather than merely awkward:
; a module's `services.py` necessarily imports its own models, repositories and
; domain, so *any* cross-module call through the sanctioned public interface
; drags those in transitively and trips the contract. The first such call — the
; Appendix C seed loader in `administration` reaching
; `apps.catalogue.services` — is what surfaced it.
;
; What is still forbidden is what the rule actually cares about: naming another
; module's internals in an import statement. `from apps.catalogue.models import
; Destination` fails here exactly as before. What is now permitted is the one
; thing §6.5 requires — `from apps.catalogue import services`.
;
; This narrows what a green run of these fourteen contracts asserts, and the
; ORM-instance property it stops covering moves to §6.5 rule 5's architecture
; test. Both are recorded in docs/adr/0014-module-privacy-contracts-check-
; direct-imports.md. The `deps-*` and layer contracts are NOT changed: those are
; genuinely about reachability and keep the default semantics.
; ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

